tio is 6.2, with a 95% confidence interval of 4.7 to 8.2. Contract [1], for 14,990 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: a pile-up of amounts just under the limit is a statistical indicator. It does not prove that any contract was broken up or that anyone acted improperly; it may reflect market prices, fixed budgets or separate needs.\nWhat can be checked: in the linked contract files, what was bought in each case and on which dates, and whether several contracts meet a single need that could have been procured at once.","origen_es":"plantilla","origen_en":"plantilla","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["A1F0pbk1Jd5SYrkJkLlFdw%3D%3D","m2f6HrG82smsNfRW6APEDw%3D%3D","l9ucosK6bTpt5r0ngvMetA%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}